title: The National Front's Structure
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1949 and month >= 11 and front_formed = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 20
on-arrival: front_formed = 1

= November 1949

The cooperation organized around
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!} and the
protest against the Sixteenth {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}
election is becoming the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}. Its
members agree on representative elections and constitutional government, but
they have not become a disciplined party.

- @narrow_program
- @coordination_committee

@narrow_program
title: Adopt a narrow constitutional program
on-arrival: front_structure = "Narrow constitutional alliance"; constitutional_legitimacy += 5; iran_party_relation += 3; independent_nationalists_relation += 3
go-to: post_event

The Front defines a limited common program around honest elections,
constitutional government, and political freedoms.

@coordination_committee
title: Remain a coordination committee
on-arrival: front_structure = "Loose coordination committee"; iran_party_dissent -= 2; toilers_dissent -= 2; independent_nationalists_dissent -= 2; religious_network_dissent -= 2; political_intelligence += 2
go-to: post_event

The cooperating circles preserve their autonomy while creating a common place
to exchange reports and coordinate immediate action.
